Yes, there is a class for crystallographic texture in the PMD Core Ontology: https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000853. This class is defined as an "intensive quality" that describes the arrangement and orientation of grains in a metallic material, typically observed through crystallographic analysis.
You can use this existing class to describe the crystal texture in your rolled copper sheet using orientation distribution function (ODF) data without needing to mint a new class.
Example RDF snippet in Turtle syntax to describe your sample's crystallographic texture:
ttl

@prefix pmd: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/> .
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .

ex:RolledCopperSheet a pmd:PMD_0000853 ;
    rdfs:comment "Crystallographic texture of a rolled copper sheet described by ODF data." .
